 ### Intersection using Rasterization
-- **Definition**: An efficient way to obtain the intersection between view-rays and the volume using OpenGL rasterization [S10].
+An efficient way to obtain the intersection between view-rays and the volume using OpenGL rasterization [S10]. A simple color cube representing the boundaries of the volume is rendered; since colors and texture coordinates are in unit space $[0,1]^3$, each color represents a 3D texture coordinate of the volume, so the color of each rasterized pixel represents the texture coordinate of the intersection of one ray with the volume [S10]. This method is used with back face culling to obtain the first intersection [S10].
 
